# Error Handling

## Backend

- Throw domain errors from services (e.g. `NotFoundError`, `ValidationError`, `ForbiddenError`, `ConflictError`).
- Map to GraphQL / HTTP with **stable error codes** (see `docs/error-handling.md`).
- Never expose stack traces, Prisma messages, or internal paths to clients.
- Unexpected errors → log + generic client message; report to Sentry when configured.
- Stripe / email / R2 failures: log with context IDs; return safe user-facing messages.

## Frontend

- Map known error codes to user-friendly copy (toast or inline).
- Network / unknown → generic retry message; do not dump raw GraphQL errors in UI.
- Forms: field-level errors from Zod; submit errors from API codes.
- Every data view needs error UI (reuse `ErrorState`) — not a blank screen.

## Do not

- `catch (e) {}` empty swallows
- `toast(error.message)` when message may be internal
- Mark order paid / stock changed in UI without confirmed API success
